  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "I fixed it in `billing/totals.py`. The existing tests pass, and I spot-checked a few half-cent inputs. I didn't have your CSV, so I haven't run the actual report.\n\n**Cause:** `line_total_cents` did its math in binary floats and then called `round()`. That goes wrong in two ways:\n- Floats can't represent many decimal values exactly. A line that should come to exactly half a cent (1.005, for example) can land just below it and round down.\n- `round()` rounds exact halves to the nearest even number, but the README says amounts round half up.\n\nEach line was already rounded to cents before summing, so a one-cent error on a line shows up in the invoice total too.\n\n**Fix:** The function now uses `Decimal` and rounds half up with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Examples from my check:\n- 1.005 gives 101 cents.\n- 2.675 gives 268 cents.\n- 0.50 with 1% tax gives 51 cents.\n\nThe old float code could get these wrong.\n\nTotals may change by a cent on the affected rows, and that is the intended correction.",
